60,3,1,talk,Kenji,,Option A is a permanent enclosure. It solves the smell if built right.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Shizue,,Option B is rotating. But Rin said the frontages are uneven.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Asuka,,Option C is managed hours. It keeps the location but adds oversight.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Rin,,Option A seems best if we can share the cost fairly.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Servas,,Option A is the most stable. The subsidy helps with the initial cost.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Rin, I agree. A permanent structure feels like a real solution.","{""words"":11,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Asuka, I worry about the maintenance of a permanent structure.","{""words"":10,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Shizue, the ward filing is strict, but it ensures quality.","{""words"":10,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Rin,,"@Servas, the cost is high, but it is one-time.","{""words"":9,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Servas,,"@Kenji, yes. It is an investment in our peace.","{""words"":9,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Kenji,,I vote for A. It ends the daily complaints.,"{""words"":9,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Shizue,,I vote for A. I hope it is well maintained.,"{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
